# Running SAT on the Cluster

This project runs inside a conda environment called SAT. On the cluster, you must load the miniforge module and initialize conda before activating the environment.

---

## Environment Setup

Before running any SAT commands or tests, execute the following in order:

    module load miniforge/25.9.1
    eval "$(conda shell.bash hook)"
    conda activate SAT

**Important:** After activating the conda environment, the system python on PATH may still point to the base miniforge Python (3.12) rather than the SAT environment Python (3.10). Always use `$CONDA_PREFIX/bin/python` to ensure you are using the correct interpreter with all dependencies installed.

---

## Running SAT

    $CONDA_PREFIX/bin/python sat/sat.py <subcommand> [args...]

For example:

    $CONDA_PREFIX/bin/python sat/sat.py aln_filter -a alignment.m8 -o filtered.m8

---

## Running Tests

    cd /mnt/labs/data/nomburg/shared/code/SAT2
    $CONDA_PREFIX/bin/python -m pytest

---

## Key Details

- Conda environment name: SAT
- Environment location: /mnt/labs/home/jnomburg/.conda/envs/SAT
- Python version in SAT env: 3.10.5
- Always use `$CONDA_PREFIX/bin/python` instead of bare `python` to avoid picking up the wrong interpreter.
- The SAT project root is the working directory when running commands (i.e. cd into the repo first).
